    "label": "thm:pac-main",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "If we set $\\gamma = \\frac12$, $N_1 = \\widetilde \\Theta \\brk[big]{\\frac{K^9}{m^8} \\log (|\\Pi|/\\delta))}$, $N_2 = \\Theta \\brk*{\\brk*{K/m \\eps + s m / \\eps^2}\\log(|\\Pi| / \\delta) }$, $T=\\Theta \\brk[big]{(K/m)^5}$,\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    then with probability at least $1-\\delta$ \\cref{alg:pac-comband} outputs $\\piout \\in \\Pi$ with $r_\\calD(\\pi^\\star) - r_\\calD(\\piout) \\leq \\eps$ using a sample complexity of \n    \\begin{align*}\n        N_1 + N_2 = O \\brk*{\\brk*{\\frac{K^9}{m^8} + \\frac{s m}{\\eps^2}} \\log \\frac{|\\Pi|}{\\delta}}.\n    \\end{align*}"
